  'tour.title':'Guided tour','tour.intro':'Walk through the main story in 9 steps. Each step switches to the right account and page for you.','tour.start':'Start the tour','tour.stepOf':'Step {n} of {total}','tour.as':'Viewing as {name}','tour.prev':'Back','tour.next':'Next','tour.exit':'Exit','tour.finish':'Finish',
  'tour.1.title':'A tenant’s home','tour.1.body':'Wei rents one bedroom in a shared house. The floor plan shows his room, the shared areas, and other tenants’ rooms as private. Open a room to see the landlord’s move-in record.',
  'tour.2.title':'Check the move-in inventory','tour.2.body':'Aisha moved in this week. She checks each room against the landlord’s record and flags anything different, with a note and a photo. After 7 days the inventory locks.',
  'tour.3.title':'The landlord’s portfolio','tour.3.body':'Priya manages two properties. They are sorted by what needs attention: urgent repairs, tenancies ending, inventories waiting for tenants.',
  'tour.4.title':'Tenancies and invite codes','tour.4.body':'Each room has its own invite code. Under Bedroom 1 Priya can see what Wei flagged when he checked the inventory.',
  'tour.5.title':'Moving a repair forward','tour.5.body':'Aisha reported mould in the shared bathroom. Priya acknowledges it, marks it in progress, then completed. Every step is logged and notifies the tenant.',
  'tour.6.title':'Housemates are affected too','tour.6.body':'Wei uses the same bathroom. Instead of reporting it again, he taps “I’m affected too”, so Priya sees how many people it affects.',
  'tour.7.title':'Move-out comparison','tour.7.body':'Lucas moves out in a few days. Priya compares Bedroom 4 with the move-in record, proposes a deduction only for real damage, and sends it.',
  'tour.8.title':'The tenant responds','tour.8.body':'Lucas agrees or disputes each deduction with a reason. If Priya hasn’t sent the check yet, go back a step and send it first.',
  'tour.9.title':'Joining with an invite code','tour.9.body':'A new tenant enters ALDER-B2 to join the vacant room. Try switching the language at the top: the whole app, including notifications, changes.',
  'tr.show':'Show translation','tr.hide':'Hide translation','tr.label':'Translation · the original above is the reference',
  'dialog.close':'Got it','term.label':'What does “{term}” mean?','term.more':'Read more on GOV.UK','term.disclaimer':'General information, not legal advice. Rules can change, so check the official guidance.',
  'term.inventory.title':'Inventory','term.inventory.body':'A record of the condition of the property and its contents at the start of a tenancy, usually with photos. It is the main evidence if there is a disagreement about damage when you move out, so check it carefully and report anything that is wrong.',
  'term.deposit.title':'Deposit protection','term.deposit.body':'In England, a landlord who takes a deposit for an assured shorthold tenancy must protect it in a government-approved scheme and give you the scheme details. At the end, any disputed amount stays protected and the scheme offers free dispute resolution.',
  'term.wearTear.title':'Fair wear and tear','term.wearTear.body':'The normal decline in condition from everyday living, such as light scuffs or faded paint. Landlords should not deduct money for it. Deductions are for damage beyond that, such as burns, stains or breakages.',
  'term.joint.title':'Joint tenancy','term.joint.body':'Several tenants sign one agreement for the whole home. Usually everyone is jointly responsible for the rent and for damage, and there is a single deposit.',
